meta {
  name: Rebuild Communities
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/communities/rebuild
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
}

docs {
  # POST /api/v1/admin/communities/rebuild

  Starts the **offline** `CommunityBuildWorkflow` on the dedicated
  `kb-graph-build` queue: GDS Leiden community detection over the
  `__Entity__` graph + a small-tier summary per community, persisted on
  `:Community` nodes. Fully decoupled from the query hot path.

  **Prerequisite for `/search/global` and `/search/drift`** — they
  map-reduce over the summaries this builds.

  ## Behaviour
  Fire-and-forget: returns the workflow id immediately; the build runs
  for minutes. Idempotent — re-running refreshes membership / summaries
  on existing `:Community` nodes.

  ## Response 202
  ```json
  { "workflow_id": "community-build-…", "status": "started" }
  ```

  ## Requires
  - Neo4j Enterprise with the GDS plugin + `gds.*` allow-listed.
  - Enough Neo4j heap (Leiden is memory-hungry — see
    `NEO4J_HEAP_MAX` in docker-compose; default 4G).

  ## Errors
  - `401` — auth. `500` — failed to start (body carries the message).
}
